          "Elohim and divine names on non-divine beings: judges (Exod 21:6), humans who carry the Name (Jer 14:9; Isa 43:7), the angel in whom the Name is (Exod 23:21), Jerusalem called “YHWH our righteousness” (Jer 33:16). A title or a Name on a messenger does not establish deity. (IA #seerahpro-bible-notes; Troki I.9)",
          "Father and Son are covenant words: Exodus 4:22-23 calls Israel God's firstborn son, and classical tafsir (Ibn Taymiyya, al-Baydawi, al-Wahidi, Ibn Qutaybah) read father and son language as mercy, closeness or cause in earlier religious speech. (IA #is-allah-the-father)",
